    "title": "fix(sm70): align QPN2 row window with the C++ mirror, tolerate non-Linear layers",
    "url": "https://github.com/1CatAI/1Cat-vLLM/pull/1441",
    "body": "Three defects hit while bringing up NVFP4 speculative decoding on V100.\n\n## 1. QPN2 row window disagrees with the C++ mirror\n\n`QPN2_DISPATCH_MAX_ROWS` is 32 in both Python copies (`nvfp4_dequant.py` and `sm70_turbomind.py`) while `csrc/sm70_turbomind/ops/nvfp4_qpn2_sm70.cu:55` uses 128.\n\nThe DFlash2 verifier issues `num_reqs * (1 + nst) = num_reqs * 8` rows, so:\n- 4 concurrent requests = 32 rows — **exactly on the limit**\n- 8 concurrent = 64 rows\n\nOne row past the limit silently switches to the dequant-to-fp16-then-cuBLAS dense fallback. That path interleaves with the device-side sampling graph's collectives and deadlocks under hot load. Observed as unbalanced GPU power — some cards idling at 160W+ while others sat near 70W — alongside:\n\n```\nNo available shared memory broadcast block found in 60 seconds\n```\n\nRaising both Python constants to 128 aligns them with the kernel that actually dispatches.\n\n## 2. Non-`LinearBase` layers crash the dense provider\n\n`UnquantizedLinearMethod.apply` read `layer._layer_execution_policy` and `layer._layer_trace` directly. Both are assigned only in `LinearBase.__init__`. `ParallelLMHead` derives from `VocabParallelEmbedding`, not `LinearBase`, so going through the dense provider raised `AttributeError` during weight loading.\n\nFalls back to the global accessors. `LinearBase` only stores a snapshot of `layer_policy()` anyway, so the semantics are identical.\n\n## 3. Quantized draft fc resolves to the wrong activation dtype\n\nAfter `prepare_nvfp4_linear`, a quantized fc exposes only an **empty uint8 weight stub**. `_dflash_context_projection_dtype()` therefore falls back to `quant_method.params_dtype` (= `model_config.dtype`), while the SM70 NVFP4 GEMM requires float16 activations:\n\n```\nnvfp4_gemm_sm70: input must be float16.\n```\n\nDetect the empty stub and force float16 rather than trusting the stub's dtype.\n\n## Testing\n\n- 4- and 8-way DFlash2 concurrency on V100: no deadlock, GPU power balanced across cards.\n- NVFP4 draft loads and warms up; no dtype assertion.\n- Models whose LM head goes through the dense provider load without AttributeError.",
