          "state": "CHANGES_REQUESTED",
          "body": "Two regressions block this head on current main. (1) Both Python QPN2 limits become128, but the actual C++ source at the reviewed base still declares kQpn2DispatchMaxRows=32 (nvfp4_qpn2_sm70.cu:41), with the existing small-row operator bounded by32. This PR does not modify that C++ file. Rows33–128 therefore cannot be admitted by assuming a128-row native implementation; keep the current bound until a matching native path and boundary/graph tests are included. (2) combine_hidden_states now takes fc_weight.dtype for every nonempty weight. Packed quantized uint8 weights are nonempty on other providers, so this casts floating hidden states to uint8; the existing _dflash_context_projection_dtype helper intentionally uses quant_method.params_dtype for packed storage. Retain that contract and scope any empty-stub SM70 correction to the actual provider. The ParallelLMHead policy/trace issue can be fixed independently. These repairs will be tracked in the quantization/sampling safety integration. Audit assisted by Codex.",
